WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.537
Unit 2 is the stages, and every
stage starts with the pre-flight.

2
00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:08.237
It reads only, and it runs
after the readers sign in.

3
00:00:08.237 --> 00:00:12.808
P F oh one reads the settings and routing
files, and fails on the wrong stage,

4
00:00:12.808 --> 00:00:15.955
no provider enabled, routing
that doesn't validate,

5
00:00:15.955 --> 00:00:19.701
or sending turned on without an
endpoint and token variable.

6
00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:22.125
Then four checks per enabled provider.

7
00:00:22.125 --> 00:00:25.125
Oh two: the provider's tool is installed.

8
00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:28.963
Oh three: the signed-in cloud
is the one the settings name,

9
00:00:28.963 --> 00:00:32.050
not another cloud, tenant,
partition or realm.

10
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:36.937
Oh four: the reader's first call works,
and for AWS that includes the support plan;

11
00:00:36.937 --> 00:00:42.050
without a qualifying plan the call fails
with a subscription required exception.

12
00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:46.012
Oh five: somebody is named to
receive the provider's notices.

13
00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.701
That's the pre-flight's link to S R eight.

14
00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:52.100
P F oh six checks that the
output root can be written.

15
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.718
And P F oh seven runs in production only:

16
00:00:54.718 --> 00:00:59.137
it fails if the test stage's evidence
wouldn't pass its stage check.

17
00:00:59.137 --> 00:01:01.900
Production can't start
until test has passed.
